<description>
Bend the single foreground lattice into a one-pixel horizontal wave anchored at its bottom row.

Input structure
- The grid has a dominant background and exactly one foreground color.
- All foreground pixels form one 4-connected lattice-like object.
- Each row inside the foreground object's bounding box contains foreground pixels.

Rule
- Keep the bottom row of the object's bounding box fixed.
- Moving upward from that bottom row, leave every other row fixed.
- Shift the intervening rows by one pixel, alternating left, right, left, right.

Key insight
- The phase of the wave is determined from the bottom of the object, not from the top.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "single-color 4-connected foreground lattice rows inside the object bbox",
  "transform": "anchor the bottom bbox row; moving upward, leave every other row fixed and shift the intervening rows one pixel left/right in alternating order"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 13-15 rows x 14-15 cols
  background: 0
  foreground: single non-zero color; one 4-connected component
  lattice:
    description: |
      Regular grid frame made of 1px-thick horizontal and vertical bars.
      All horizontal bars span the full bbox width. All vertical bars span the full bbox height.
      Non-bar rows contain only the vertical-bar columns (all identical).
    n_horizontal_bars: 2-4 (top/bottom edges + 0-2 interior)
    n_vertical_bar_groups: 2-3 (left/right edges + 0-1 interior)
    cell_width: 1-4 (gap between adjacent vertical bars, uniform)
    cell_height: 2-11 (gap between adjacent horizontal bars, uniform)
    bar_thickness: 1 [observed]; one example has a 2px-wide vertical bar group
    object_height: 7-13, object_width: 5-9
  margins:
    left: >=1, right: >=1 (hard requirement for wave shift to stay in bounds)
    observed: left 2-4, right 2-6, top 1-4, bottom 1-3
  transform:
    description: |
      Wave-shift rows relative to the bottom row of the object bbox.
      Bottom row (distance 0) is fixed. Even-distance rows are fixed.
      Odd-distance rows shift by 1px: d=1 left, d=3 right, d=5 left, d=7 right, ...
    shifted_rows_must_not_collide: true (after clearing old positions, new positions must be bg)

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (input is the constrained object; transform is deterministic)
  steps:
    - Pick grid dims (13-15 x 14-15), fg color, bg=0
    - Choose n_hbars (2-4) and n_vbar_groups (2-3)
    - Choose uniform cell_width (1-4) and cell_height (2-11)
    - Compute object size from bars+cells; ensure object fits with >=2 margin on each side
    - Place the lattice on a bg grid at a random position respecting margins
    - Verify the lattice forms one 4-connected component
    - Output is produced by applying the wave shift; no generation needed
  constraints:
    - left and right margins >= 2 guarantees shifted output stays in bounds
    - Keep object_height 7-13 and object_width 5-9 by constraining bar/cell counts
